algorithms.pseudocode:
Algorithm: GreedyHittingSet(U, F, delta)
Input: Universe U, family F of subsets, density threshold delta
Output: Hitting set H subset U

H <- empty set
while F is not empty:
    // Averaging lemma: some element hits >= delta fraction
    a* <- argmax_{a in U} |{S in F : a in S}|
    H <- H union {a*}
    F <- {S in F : a* not in S}
return H

Complexity: O(k * |U| * |F|) where k = ceil(log_{1/(1-delta)} |F|)
For delta = 3/4: k = ceil(log_4 |F|) = O(log |F|)
